    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `checkDigit` field as a Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (an `int32`, 0\u20139, `readOnly`), documented as a Luhn check digit over the customerCode digits. This drives generation of the `checkDigit` field on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and a `checkDigit(Owner)` helper. It's a derived (not stored) value that follows the same conventions as the other computed fields like `membershipNumber` and `initials`. The Luhn implementation matches the standard algorithm the test uses: iterate the customerCode right-to-left, skipping non-digits, doubling every other digit (starting from the rightmost digit) and subtracting 9 when >9, then returning `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`. Returns `null` when there's no customer code.\n\n**Verification:** `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact `checkDigit` \u2014 passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test, 0 failures).",
