    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `checkDigit` derivation follows the mapper's established pattern exactly: a self-contained `default` method wired via a `@Mapping(... expression=...)` entry, sitting alongside the other derived-field helpers (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, etc.). This interface is already, by design, the home for owner-derived presentation fields, so adding another one is coherent and additive rather than turning it into a catch-all.\n\nDetails that make it fit naturally:\n- Null-guarding style (`owner == null || owner.getCustomerCode() == null`) matches the sibling methods, and it's placed next to `membershipNumber`, the other `customerCode`-based derivation.\n- The Luhn computation is entirely local to the one field it serves \u2014 no shared state, no duplication with existing logic, nothing that belongs in a separate utility given how the rest of the file keeps each derivation inline.\n- The OpenAPI schema addition is placed logically among the other read-only derived fields and mirrors their documentation style.\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
